Wikia as a policy will not shut down the old site. That means some
editors will move to the new site, and a few won't notice/want the
move and will try to keep the old one alive. If the editing community
splits, the danger for us is that Google might keep bringing traffic
to the old site. Given how well we control incoming links and how
clear the vote is so far, that outcome seems unlikely. But I really
want to be honest about the potential downsides of a move.

If you can find a succinct way to express this concern more clearly,
please add it to the discussion on the wiki.

(I know only one case out of many where the admins of a moving wiki
got Wikia to shut the old site down, much later.)


